    {
      "id": "table-4",
      "line": 441,
      "heading_context": "## Gotchas from C#",
      "headers": [
        "C# behavior",
        "JavaScript behavior",
        "Consequence"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "`==` is value equality (for strings)",
          "`==` coerces types",
          "Use `===` always"
        ],
        [
          "`null` — one null",
          "Two: `null` AND `undefined`",
          "Check with `== null`"
        ],
        [
          "No automatic type coercions",
          "`\"5\" - 3 = 2`",
          "Arithmetic coercions are quiet"
        ],
        [
          "`Dictionary<K,V>` has only string-compatible keys",
          "`{}` keys are strings/symbols; use `Map` for anything else",
          "Object keys coerce to string"
        ],
        [
          "Non-virtual methods are stable",
          "`this` can change based on call site",
          "Arrow functions or `.bind(this)`"
        ],
        [
          "Integer division: `5/2 = 2`",
          "`5/2 = 2.5` (one number type)",
          "Use `Math.floor(5/2)` for int division"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "table-5",
      "line": 456,
      "heading_context": "## Decision Cheat Sheet",
      "headers": [
        "Use",
        "When"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "`===`",
          "Always, for equality checks"
        ],
        [
          "`==`",
          "Only one valid idiom: `x == null` to check for null-or-undefined in one shot"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "table-6",
      "line": 465,
      "heading_context": "## Decision Cheat Sheet",
      "headers": [
        "Use",
        "When"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "`const`",
          "Default — for any binding you don't reassign (objects/arrays can still mutate internally)"
        ],
        [
          "`let`",
          "When you need to reassign the binding (loop counter, accumulated result)"
        ],
        [
          "`var`",
          "Never in new code — function-scoped and hoisted to the top of the function, causing non-obvious bugs"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "table-7",
      "line": 475,
      "heading_context": "## Decision Cheat Sheet",
      "headers": [
        "Use",
        "When"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Arrow `() => {}`",
          "Default for callbacks, methods passed as values, anything that needs lexical `this`"
        ],
        [
          "`function` declaration",
          "Top-level named functions you want hoisted; methods that need their own `this` (e.g. event handlers that reference `this.element`)"
        ],
        [
          "`function` expression",
          "Rarely — named function expressions for recursion or stack traces"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "table-8",
      "line": 493,
      "heading_context": "## Decision Cheat Sheet",
      "headers": [
        "Use",
        "When"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "`{}` plain object",
          "Keys are known strings/identifiers, shape is fixed, JSON serialization needed"
        ],
        [
          "`Map`",
          "Keys are dynamic, non-string keys (objects, numbers), need insertion-order iteration, need `.size`"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "table-9",
      "line": 502,
      "heading_context": "## Decision Cheat Sheet",
      "headers": [
        "Use",
        "When"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "`async/await`",
          "Default — reads as sequential code, error handling via try/catch"
        ],
        [
          "`.then()` chains",
          "Parallel fan-out patterns (`Promise.all`, `Promise.race`); piping transformations without needing intermediate variables"
        ],
        [
          "Mixed",
          "`async` function calling `await Promise.all([...])` — best of both"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
